# Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale eu
# (https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),
# transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as the night band.
# Surface: inessive 'gauean' — at night -- the deictic form these phrases use.
# Source: Wiktionary, gau — https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gau (inessive gauean)
gauean
# absolutive "gaua" after a -ko day word ("atzoko gaua"): Wiktionary, gaua.
# "gau honetan" (in this night) is tonight: eu.wikipedia "Walpurgis gaua"
# ("gau honetan sorginak bildu ohi baitziren"); Wiktionary, honetan.
gaua
gau honetan
